# One PAC instruction at a site (pac::sign's `pacda`, auth's `autda`,
# strip's `xpacd`; verus/seams/sys-pac-*.md), in one configuration:
# Non-secure EL0, FEAT_PAuth on, the PAC traps off (SCR_EL3.API, and
# HCR_EL2.API or E2H+TGE), the translation control pinned to Linux's for
# one VA size, SCTLR (EnDA among it) symbolic. run.sh prepends the insn
# line and substitutes @D@ (the destination register). ComputePAC, the
# PAC algorithm, is uninterpreted: what follows holds for any function of
# its arguments.
abstract ComputePAC
writes @D@
no-mem-write
mem-reads 0
flags-preserved
# Every path falls through: no trap, no fault, no branch.
assert (= final._PC (bvadd init._PC #x0000000000000004))
